              "line": 105,
              "message": "T006 is not executable as written: its description names only “Test-obligation regression fixtures and bounded calibration path” and “root-host validation”, without a target file or symbol. Name the concrete fixture/test and validation targets.",
              "severity": "P2"
            },
            {
              "category": "upstream restatement",
              "file": "track/items/2026-09-11-test-obligation-verifier-context-integrity/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 6,
              "message": "Sections S1-S4 restate upstream behavior contracts instead of limiting the plan sections to target, operation, and anchor. Examples include “make the existing structured specification element the normalized verifier input”, “invalidating old Pass and Fail values alike”, and “section-aware exclusion semantics”. Remove the behavioral rationale from these section descriptions; retain concrete targets, operations, and anchors.",
              "severity": "P2"
            },
            {
              "category": "upstream restatement",
              "file": "track/items/2026-09-11-test-obligation-verifier-context-integrity/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 67,
              "message": "T002-T006 contain upstream contract restatements beyond the permitted target/operation/anchor form, including “retain missing-material pending behavior”, “map stale ... to ... pending”, “exclusions are not affirmative requirements”, “preserve fail-closed configuration diagnostics”, and the extensive regression-behavior list in T006. Cite the targets and anchors without repeating the spec behavior prose; see .harness/policies/no-upstream-restatement.md.",
              "severity": "P2"
            },
            {
              "category": "pre-implementation split proposal",
              "file": "track/items/2026-09-11-test-obligation-verifier-context-integrity/impl-plan.json",
              "line": 105,
              "message": "Before implementation starts, split T006 into independently verifiable units: verifier-lane/spec-section regressions (IN-01/IN-02/AC-01/AC-02), stale Pass/Fail evaluate-check-results freshness (IN-04/IN-05/AC-03), and normal cache-preserving binary/root-host validation (AC-04). Each unit can be tested independently and currently has a single broad task boundary.",
              "severity": "P2"
            }
          ],
